doing pilot studies with us now at several schools. But most recently, we did tango games with the entire incoming class at Harvard. So the class of 2029, over a thousand students, and we see positive effects on all of our outcome measures. So the one I'm most proud of, or the combination I'm most proud of, you may have heard of this in the news, Harvard does lean liberal. So, you know, about 80% of students identify as some kind of liberal, but about 20% do identify as some kind of conservative. And what we found is that when liberals played with the conservatives at Harvard, the liberals showed a seven-point increase in their feeling of less cold and more warm towards conservative students. And the conservative said that they had a five-point increase in the extent to which they said they felt comfortable voicing controversial opinions at Harvard.
现在在几所学校进行试点研究。但最近，我们与哈佛大学的整个新生班级进行了探戈游戏。所以2029届，超过一千名学生，我们在所有的结果指标上都看到了积极的影响。所以我最自豪的一个，或者我最自豪的组合，你可能在新闻中听说过，哈佛确实倾向于自由派。所以，你知道，大约80%的学生认同某种自由派，但大约20%的学生确实认同某种保守派。我们发现，当自由派与哈佛的保守派一起玩时，自由派对保守派学生的感觉从冷淡到温暖，显示出七分的增长。而保守派表示，他们对自己说在哈佛表达有争议观点时感到舒适的程度增加了五分。

